battlefield 4 is a game that i hold  really close to my heart from constant  changes and improvements over the years  to help stabilize rough early launch  issues to fantastic spectacles in an  open sandbox  and an actually halfway decent campaign  what's up all  i'm david and this video is going to be  focused on battlefield 4 but we have  so many more battlefield videos cooking  up for 2042  so definitely subscribe and hit that  bell button so you'll always be in the  know your feedback means a lot to me  but for now let's take a quick trip  through memory lane  [Music]  i originally got into battlefield with  1942 on a garbage windows xp pc  playing against bots and staring at the  intro cutscene  absolutely stunned and convinced that  video games  reached their peak and looking realistic  now most of my time was spent running  around and looking for the planes and  various vehicles and just  cruising around my childhood best friend  was extremely into battlefield vietnam  and later on battlefield 2 but all i  knew was the prestige of the name and  experiencing those games second hand  fast forward to after being swept away  by modern warfare 2 and other entries in  the call of duty franchise throughout  middle in high school  and battlefield was a little absent for  my fps life  in 2013 battlefield 4 was my first real  experience with the series  when i actually played games as a hobby  now i had just received the xbox one  complete with the shitty kinect for my  birthday  and the only games that i had at launch  were forza 5 and ryze son of rome  i was desperate for something to play  and since i loved shooters  and was an early adopter of buying  digital games through the xbox store i  stumbled on battlefield 4.  now at this point i dove into the  campaign i know it's not the biggest  thing players go for nor is it the  primary mode battlefield is known for  but keep in mind back in 2013 before all  the battle royales and live service or  free-to-play games were everywhere  most shooters put as strong an emphasis  on single-player  as they did their multiplayer well no  with shooters you had about a 6 to 12  hour campaign  and then if you weren't an achievement  hunter you'd go into a hopefully  fun multiplayer with your buddies  battlefield 4  had the luxury of both by the time the  xbox one and ps4 generations was in full  swing  split screen co-op was quickly becoming  a distant memory  you either had to use xbox live and  separate consoles or you could just toss  the controller around and take turns  between lives which is what my buddies  and i did  and i mean all of my college doormates  and i played we didn't even play to win  or get a lot of kills and rock a wicked  kd  i actually didn't even know what good  kds were until years later when i  started going hardcore in a destiny in  call of duty pvp  what i do remember was when i first got  the game my roommate kept laughing when  i die  and at first i got pissed i thought he  was laughing at me when in fact  he was laughing at the situation and the  ways that the deaths were happening  i mean you're flying around crashing  into other jets or buildings you're on a  quad bike and you fly over a land mine  and blow up and explode like  that is funny we pass the controller  around and try to do dumb stunts  like really dumb like ignoring the  objectives and just  base jumping off of buildings trying to  do tricks on jets and fly as close to  the skyscrapers as you dare  knowing damn well if you mess up it'd be  another 10 minutes before you'd find  another jet  jump out of a plane and try to parachute  into a helicopter with your squad you  know only try to run people over with  the quad bike  just absolute silliness directly tied to  my fascination with battlefield 4 was  what allowed all of that crazy insanity  to happen in the first place  keep in mind a lot of mainstream aaa  games throughout the xbox 360 and  playstation 3 generation  were fairly linear and restrictive with  where you could go and what you could do  this was especially true when it comes  to multiplayer matches where you  effectively had a few objectives like  killing bad guys and going to capture  points  it's honestly a good time to mention  that every time i talk about battlefield  4 spectacle and moments of grandeur from  this point on  there's this equal amount of just comedy  like pure silliness and that separates  battlefield 4 from its successors in a  big way  battlefield 1 and 5 seem more focused on  trying to create this  gritty serious type atmosphere which is  fine i mean i love playing them both but  if there is  one thing about battlefield 4's  multiplayer it's that it never took  itself too seriously  and i mean just look at this how could  you keep a straight face  battlefield's contribution as a series  was sure do your normal objectives  but we won't tell you how you're  supposed to do it want to plant a tank  on a flag point  fine want to airmail your jet and then  parachute away into enemy territory  no problem want to just chill with your  squad and repair their vehicles  congratulations you're my new best  friend battlefield 4 stayed true to that  philosophy  and was just so open in establishing an  arena of creating as much mayhem  as possible battlefield truly loves  chaos  and battlefield 4 would up the ante with  levolution  now we go deep into why levolution was  so crazy in its own right in another  video  but to sum it up briefly here levolution  was a turning point in conquest matches  where the map would distinctly change  after being triggered by the players in  many instances  the iconic revolution in battlefield is  the siege of shanghai building  collapsing over objective point c  everyone has seen that one  and during the early launch period a  levolution infuriatingly usually ended  and getting booted from the server  because it was just too much for the  game to handle  but as patches came in and the game  started to stabilize  they quickly became highlights for me  the first time i saw  the heinen resort crumble in front of me  or that massive paracel storm aircraft  carrier  spectacularly crashed on shore all that  will always stay with me  and all this is to say that battlefield  4 not only had an  exceptionally grand and open sandbox but  this idea of spectacle  and silliness was everywhere and the  game encouraged an environment where  getting a high kd  was the last thing on my mind rather i  was here purely to tag along for those  battlefield moments these memories i had  with battlefield 4 give it an extremely  special place in my heart  and by far are the top reasons i will  always love this game  but whereas all this was subjective to  my own experience there are also a dozen  reasons why battlefield 4 was so damn  good from a support standpoint as well  and most of it involves at how  fine-tuned the gameplay became  to understand the leaps battlefield 4  has made you need to know what the game  was like at launch  battlefield 4 was a disaster with bugs  and net code issues  but with laser focus from dice that  persisted and was iterated upon  it eventually overcame a lot of its  struggles though not until  nearly a year later after its launch  which definitely  did not sit well with the community at  first it's worth noting that when we  talk about battlefield 4 as of right now  we're factoring in so much added post  launch content and dlc  a long list of varied maps an incredible  lineup of fun and distinct weapons and  weapon archetypes  most importantly there are a lot of  different game modes which always ensure  some degree of novelty and change  for those who are easily bored by  repetition if you're lukewarm on the  maps  that's fine since there always seemed to  be a new build strategy or even vehicle  that you can master  and for those premium and dlc owners the  content kept growing  there were so many broken metas and  ridiculous strategies used but despite  that hilarity  or frustration of those eras dice has  always been pretty solid about sandbox  tuning and the current state of the  battlefield 4 meta feels really good  another thing battlefield 4 has is a  very passionate community  which is reflected in the custom servers  that are available want to play only on  gold mud railway  no worries want a 24 7 operation locker  64 player server  here you go you maniac  right they were serviced with fast  respawn rates and others that harbored  fun spaces for battlefield fanatics  to always go back to and all of this  culminated in a complete battlefield  experience  that ironed out the launchier kinks and  allowed pc and console players to  properly enjoy the experience of a 64  player server  dialed up to an 11. the biggest reason  battlefield 4 is so  good is that it passes the basic smell  test  is this game fun and the answer being  absolutely which is really all that  matters at the end of the day  sure for some especially non-battlefield  veterans  it can take a minute to get adjusted to  the fact that  everything looks grey or brown or that  enemies tend to blend in with the  environment  but all of that quickly subsides a lot  of people like to compare battlefield 4  as a half step improvement over  battlefield 3.  and to that i say it really depends on  which one you grew up with  one thing i will say is that battlefield  4 had a much better balance between  grounded firefights  and absolute action movie mayhem than  battlefield 3 for starters  in battlefield 4 you wouldn't have your  entire vision get all blurry and  suppressed from taking damage for  instance  and the progression system in  battlefield 4 felt rewarding  rank-ups were awesome and unlocking new  cosmetics and skins for your guns to  unleash on your enemies  was just an added plus battlefield might  be the only shooter that doesn't exclude  any style of gamer either  the fact that i a casual love it so much  alongside the die hards  isn't the only proof battlefield does  not require what call of duty requires  which is rkd fast twitch skills above  all else you might not be going off on a  massive kill streak in battlefield all  the time  but no matter what kind of player you  are every action you take dramatically  contributes to your team  particularly in conquest in battlefield  it is not  uncommon to go several minutes without  firing a single shot  particularly if you're not playing  assault and diving in objectives  or if you're on a large map hell i've  seen helicopter pilots  just hover as high as possible over the  middle of the map to act as an extra  spawn zone  where we just spawn in only to jump out  immediately  to get a better vantage point mid map  battlefield gets better the more  imaginative that you get  and that might be the most important  reason why this game is so good  now that battlefield 2042 has been  announced and returned to a near future  setting  if you need something to get your feet  wet while waiting it is a perfect time  to return to battlefield 4.  the game is still going strong and has  plenty of fun servers  and i guarantee it will be a good time  now that i've gone a little misty eyed  on this game i want to hear your stories  as well  tell me what you remember fondly about  battlefield 4 or tell me what you're  excited about for 2042 in the comments  i read all of them thanks for watching  [Music]  so  you

